# tools/structure_witness.rish -- a general structuring element proves itself on metal (Season G).
#
# Season G (Open Media Primitives) -- the generalization the morphology family descends from. image/morphology.rye grows
# dilate (max) and erode (min) over a SQUARE (2r+1)x(2r+1) element, separable and fast. A square is only the simplest
# element: a mask cleanup often wants a CROSS (the 4-neighborhood, no corners), a LINE (a directional element), a DISK, or
# the paired templates a hit-or-miss transform reads. Every one is the SAME two verbs with only the element's SHAPE changed.
# So this rung generalizes the window from "a radius" to "a set of (dx, dy) offsets," and the square element proves it.
#
# The crux this witness proves is that the general verb CONTAINS the special one: a square offset set reproduces
# morphology.dilate and morphology.erode byte-for-byte at radius 1 and 2 on a colored translucent field, exactly as
# convolve_n's widest kernel reproduces convolve. On metal: a cross element grows a dot into a plus and leaves the diagonal
# corners black where a square would light them (the shape matters); a directional horizontal-line element widens a vertical
# line horizontally yet leaves every column whole; the DUALITY law holds for the symmetric cross; a single-offset element is
# the identity; alpha morphs like any channel; the result round-trips through the open QOI codec byte-for-byte; an empty
# element, an over-max element, and an empty source refuse by name; the same dilate is deterministic. No network, no key, no
# funds -- the cross, the line, the disk, and the hit-or-miss template a surface reaches for the day a square is the wrong
# shape, on our own open geometry.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/structure_witness.rish

say "structure: Language EN -- Season G general structuring element; an RGBA image reshaped by dilate (max) and erode (min) over an arbitrary offset set, the general the square morphology is one shape of."
say "structure: Style Radiant -- the general contains the special: a square offset set reproduces the separable morphology verbs byte-for-byte; a cross, a line, and a disk are their own small sets; erode and dilate stay DUALS under complement for a symmetric element."
say "structure: Lens TAME -- u32 in-memory counts, the offset count bounded and refused by name; each function states its invariants positively; the source and element guarded once up front so a refusal allocates nothing; every offset clamps at the border so no gather reads outside the buffer; the accumulators are u8 (a rank of bytes is a byte) so no arithmetic can wrap; no network, no key, no funds."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "image/bin/structure"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p image/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build image/structure.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "structure: build failed -- ${build.err}"

let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "structure: selftest exited non-zero -- ${selftest.out}"

let out = trim selftest.out
say "structure: ${out}"

assert selftest.out contains "GREEN image-structure" else "structure: selftest did not print the GREEN line"

say "structure: GREEN -- dilate and erode reshape an RGBA image over a general element, the square offset set equal to the separable morphology verbs byte-for-byte, the cross shape leaving its diagonals black, the duality law holding, on metal."
